# Bling API Reference Links

## Source of Truth

All endpoints, parameters, and response shapes must match [Bling API v3 reference](https://developer.bling.com.br/referencia).

Changelog tracking: [Bling changelogs](https://developer.bling.com.br/changelogs) (README cites API version alignment).

## `@see` in Entity Methods

Every entity method in `index.ts` includes a `@see` pointing to the exact operation in the Bling reference.

Copy URL structure from an existing method in the same resource or a similar one:

- `src/entities/camposCustomizados/index.ts` — custom fields
- `src/entities/pedidosVendas/index.ts` — orders with actions
- `src/entities/nfses/index.ts` — fiscal documents

## Class-Level `@see`

Entity class JSDoc links to the resource group anchor (e.g. `#/Contatos`, `#/Campos%20Customizados`).

## README Entity List

`README.md` maintains the consumer-facing checklist of `bling.<getter>` accessors. Update when adding a new module to `src/bling.ts`.

## Authentication Docs

OAuth and token acquisition are **not** implemented in this library. Point consumers to:

- `README.md` — authentication section
- `https://developer.bling.com.br/aplicativos#tokens-de-acesso`
- `demo/` — working authorization demo

## Endpoint Verification

Before merging new operations:

1. Confirm HTTP verb and path in Bling reference.
2. Map to correct `repository.*` method (`architecture/repository-layer.mdc`).
3. Match query/body field names exactly to Bling (Portuguese camelCase).

## Versioning

Package major version 5.x targets API v3 (`README.md`). Breaking Bling API changes may require interface updates across affected `interfaces/` files.
